+# Generated akimbo for Sundial v0.6
+
+This companion targets Dawn 1.7.2 at base commit
+`e801e23e22248dce35731a340395510ca73e8c72` and game build 86657. Generated
+weapons use descriptor schema 5 and an installed capability bound to the exact
+runtime and executable hashes. The retained weapon-specific adapters remain in
+the source; new generated registrations advertise these separate capabilities:
+
+| Adapter | Generated behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| 7 | The retained, strictly qualified SMG rig and independent single-event firing path. |
+| 10 | Source-qualified common gun rigs with private marker bones, native firing-origin groups, ordinary or tube reloads, and donor-derived visual attachments. |
+| 11 | Digital, uncharged finite bursts. Each hand owns a complete native burst; both-held input alternates complete bursts with an unhalved native inter-round handoff. |
+
+Each generated hand has its own magazine, reload state and native HUD counter.
+Reload policy 3 selects the lower magazine, left on a partial tie. Both can reload
+only when both are empty; a fresh request may add the second empty hand without
+restarting the first timer. Logical handle/owner/model identity survives validated
+native storage moves. Finite and enabled infinite-reserve policies preserve finite
+hand magazines and checked native transfers.
+
+Adapter 11 requires a private core in the verified runtime append (package 01BB,
+entry 6468 onward) or authored standalone window 0AA0 through 0CFF, plus an emitted
+package pin. Inherited stock-overlay entries cannot authorize startup interception.
+A private core waits for full owner/presentation qualification before its native
+trigger or phase runs. Paid queue receipts retain their hand through continuation,
+reload interruption and phase exit. Semantic failures refuse further execution.
+
+This is structural compatibility, not a weapon-name allowlist. Unsupported charge,
+continuous-fire and sword ownership remain refused; the isolated charge prototypes
+are not production adapters. Native signatures, typed source graphs, animation
+ranges, firing costs/counts, owners and generations are checked before mutation.
+
+The current Release checkpoint passed source-only regressions, production loader
+checks, and initialization/shutdown with 33 actual emitted profiles and genuine
+package bytes. The non-game lifecycle harness correctly refused game-hook
+attachment. Earlier SMG placement/firing/reload paths were exercised in game;
+this schema-5 cross-family/burst checkpoint still needs in-game validation of its
+firing, cadence, reloads, hand poses, particles and native counter presentation.
+See [portable tests](../../../../unit/AKIMBO-TESTS.md) for reproducible synthetic
+checks and their limits. Recorded captures, packages, runtime binaries, PDBs and
+account data are not part of this source companion.
+
+The dated sections below are retained implementation history. Their acceptance
+notes and fixed donor identities describe those earlier adapters, not validation
+of newly generated weapons.
+## Sturm & Drang Akimbo S2: handle identity, the input-pass driver, a stable remap, the aim (2026-09-26, awaiting gameplay)
+
+The user on S1: left click inconsistent (sometimes nothing, sometimes Sturm),
+right click sometimes scopes in Sturm, the perks work. The S1 session log
+(INTEGRATION-S2) showed why: the S&D components are RELOCATED in memory every few
+seconds with the same handles (sturm_self / drang_self / the content handle fixed,
+the root addresses changing: 50 discoveries in ~9 min, 23 refused), so the
+raw-address cache went stale, eligibility lapsed, the remap fell back to native
+bindings, and the H1 driver starved (no_tick 135 of 270 presses, H1 gaps of 2 s).
+binding_tid == h1_tid == native_fire_tid for the whole session. What changed
+(INTEGRATION-S2 decisions 1-4; retained-research/s2\BUILD.md):
+- Identity by handle (sturm_drang_discovery.h relocate): the input pass
+  re-resolves both roots and the active component by handle every pass through
+  the checked resolver (25 checked copies) and re-checks their identity pins; a
+  moved part is followed (a new revision, the hooks' pointers updated), never a
+  discovery, never a cancel. fast_revalidate and recheck follow every part they
+  read the same way. Only a handle that stops resolving or a failed pin drops the
+  cache (relocate result=lost -> discover). firing_hook routes S&D barrels by
+  barrel+0x98 == the cached self (barrel_identity), not by a cached pointer.
+- The driver runs in the input pass (Driver::frame, called at the end of every
+  armed InputPass::pass through the environment's drive()): shots, cadence, the
+  ammo/reload clock, spend and FX, every frame; no press waits on H1. H1 is an
+  observer (counts, the probe, the fire thread); keep-awake is retired
+  (kKeepAwake false). Every native call needs the current thread == the thread
+  native firing was last seen on (Sturm's or Drang's H1, a native S&D emission;
+  Shared::fireTid), else refuse fire_thread (the press stays pending).
+- The remap follows the drawn weapon (RemapState::drawn): the handle-resolved
+  active component names Sturm -> the S&D table; another weapon -> native at
+  once; no active evidence -> the presented private model, then 0.5 s of grace.
+  RMB = Sturm 111, zoom 116, LMB never Sturm's trigger while S&D is drawn, also
+  while discovery refreshes. Quiet only for a UI / lost focus.
+- The aim (sturm_drang_firing.h aim): Drang's shot leaves the left muzzle along
+  the ray to the crosshair point 20 m out (the export path publishes the camera
+  rotation and the view origin, Signals::publish_aim); parallel to the camera if
+  the view origin does not fit, the S1 direction if no fresh aim frame.
+- Log: ev=sd stage=relocate (moved/lost), stage=remap (every table change and
+  its evidence), stage=s2 every 10 s (driver_frames, presses, shots,
+  discoveries, relocs, reloc_lost, shot_relocs, remap_changes,
+  native_while_drawn, fire_thread_refusals, aim sources), the threads line
+  (driver=input driver_tid fire_tid fire_src same_driver_fire h1_observed), the
+  shot line (aim= aim_delta_deg muzzle_delta_deg aim_age_ms relocated= driver=input
+  fire_tid=), refuse reason=fire_thread with the tids.
+- Tests: Dawn\unit\sturm_drang_s2_tests.cpp replays the S1 session on a synthetic
+  game image (sturm_drang_synthetic.h: the real Pump, relocate and
+  fast_revalidate); compiled with /DSD_BASELINE_S1 against 6585417 it fails
+  (18 discoveries, LMB->Sturm and RMB zoom on 2138 of 7201 frames, 19 shots for
+  149 presses), on S2 it passes.
+
+## Sturm & Drang Akimbo S1: the review fixes (2026-09-26, awaiting gameplay)
+
+Four adversarial reviews of the S1 build (crash, regression, gameplay, tests;
+retained-research/review-*.md). Every verdict and its evidence is in
+retained-research/build\FIX.md. What changed:
+- Keep-awake and Drang's refill run only while S&D is eligible (drawn,
+  presented, focused, no UI): eligibility ends on the first pass that cannot
+  fire, and after 100 ms with no pass at all. The quiet grace keeps the bindings
+  only (crash F1).
+- Drang's own H1 and our emission/spend/FX hold an EmitGate (a Dekker handshake
+  with a bounded 1 ms wait, sturm_drang_runtime.h): the driver withdraws while
+  Drang's H1 is in flight (refuse drang_h1, the press stays pending); Drang's H1
+  waits while our emission runs on another worker; only a wait that runs out
+  latches L8. post_update_hook hands Drang's H1 to sturm_drang::drang_h1 before
+  its original (crash F2).
+- The cached barrels count only while barrel+0x98 still names the cached root
+  self (native_barrel, drang_h1): a weapon re-allocated at a cached address keeps
+  its firing::dispatch route; the magazine observers are cleared 1 s after S&D
+  is gone and republished when it is back (regression F1). Sturm counts as
+  active only on positive evidence (the cache's active component, else S&D
+  presented), so a swap before discovery hands native bindings back at once
+  (regression F2).
+- The driver-thread pin is per H1 invocation (taken under busy_, released at
+  its end; moves counted and logged pin_moved): Sturm's H1 moving between job
+  workers never starves Drang or strands a refill; a refill stuck 0.5 s on
+  eligible ticks is cancelled and the empty reload restarts (gameplay F1). An
+  empty Drang restarts its reload by itself after a re-arm (F7).
+- Sturm's selector class is published by the export path; a fresh draw,
+  put-away, sprint or unknown action (melee, finisher) refuses a Drang shot
+  (sturm_state); during Sturm's own reload CC29C0 is logged only, so the guns
+  stay independent. The shot line logs sturm_state, action and aim_delta_deg
+  (origin vs the world camera) (gameplay F2).
+- Every LMB press records whether the OS cursor shows (cursor= on the shot line,
+  cursor_presses in the summary): S1 evidence for clicks inside game menus (F3).
+  A press while no armed H1 tick came for 150 ms counts refuse no_tick (F4).
+- After any entry into S&D, slot-0 fire stays unbound until RMB has been seen up
+  once (Remap::sturmDrangHeld): an RMB held across the switch never becomes a
+  ghost Sturm shot (F5).
+- Drang's slide cycle writes p[74]/p[78] only while Sturm's own parts rest at
+  bind (1 mm / 1 degree), so a Drang shot never freezes Sturm's reload or fire
+  clip (F6). A native Drang emission while S&D is eligible is a ghost: counted
+  (drang_ghosts) and L1 (F9).
+- The install decision is the pure runtime::install_plan() (guard groups, kill
+  file, plan); native_akimbo_barrel() refuses the S&D identity outright.
+- The threads line adds pin_moves, drang_h1_waits and drang_h1_overlaps; the
+  summary adds cursor_presses, sturm_disabled_reload and drang_ghosts; the fixed
+  log buffers use bounded appends (crash F3). sd_ammo lines carry tid= (crash F6).
+- Exception to ruling 2 (crash F5, pre-existing for every akimbo model): the
+  shared identify_controller / correct_export plumbing still reads through
+  local_read for S&D frames; only the S&D selector, clock, controller, output and
+  camera words go through checked_read.
+- New tests: Dawn\unit\sturm_drang_review_tests (every finding, incl. the
+  reviewers' LateWorld, RateWorld, LockWorld, hysteresis, FX frame and guard-row
+  cases), sturm_drang_runtime_native_tests (the runtime adapters on a fake
+  module with RVA stubs), sturm_drang_identity_tests; T8 gained the model tag
+  and both definitions; the runtime tests lost their tautologies.
+
+## Sturm & Drang Akimbo S1: Drang fires (2026-09-26, builder 2 of 2, awaiting gameplay)
+
+The firing and ammo half of S1 (design-firing S1 + design-ammo P0 with every
+critique-firing / critique-ammo fix and the INTEGRATION-S1 rulings 1-14). RMB
+fires Sturm natively; LMB fires Drang through Drang's own barrel; no ADS. The
+pure rules live in sturm_drang_firing.h (remap, trigger, cadence, left origin,
+probe/keep-awake, log budget), sturm_drang_ammo.h (Drang's magazine pins,
+spend verdict, reload clock, refill plan) and sturm_drang_driver.h (the driver
+and the input pass, templated so the unit tests inject fakes);
+sturm_drang.cpp binds them to the game.
+
+Input (binding_hook, one pass at slot 0 / action 0; ruling 5 and 13):
+- Pre-gate: nothing runs unless S&D was presented within 100 ms (the
+  session's seen stamp) or the remap is still armed. A non-S&D player pays two
+  atomic loads: no clock, no focus query, no 343C30 sample, no pump, no read.
+- Remap (S&D drawn, focused, no UI, the cache not saying another weapon is
+  active): slot 0 fire -> 111 (RMB = Sturm's native fire), slot 1 fire -> 116,
+  zoom 1/2 -> 116, reload 6 native (slot-0 fire stays 116 until RMB is seen up
+  once after entering S&D). A transient ineligibility while armed keeps fire and
+  zoom unbound for up to 1 s (quiet); then native. After a latch the
+  table stays (RMB Sturm, LMB nothing); only the kill file, the guards or 8
+  unreadable mouse samples (L9) give native bindings.
+- LMB = buttons[0] of the same 343C30 sample (checked read). Edges carry a
+  session-monotonic serial; every reset bumps the epoch inside sample(); the
+  driver primes to the serial at the bump; release-to-arm.
+- The discovery pump (128 cells / 0.25 ms per pass) runs while S&D is drawn
+  and no cache is valid; an accepted cache publishes the Sturm barrel (arming
+  H1), Drang's barrel and both magazines for the pointer-compare observers.
+
+Driver (H1 = CCF6A0, after the original, only for the armed S&D Sturm barrel):
+- Probe once per session (2 s from the first arm) against the binding-pass
+  heartbeat: ticking (>= 20/s, gap <= 100 ms, >= 80 % of the passes), sparse or
+  none. Keep-awake (H1 returns true) only after a sparse/none verdict, only
+  while S&D is eligible (review fix: never through the quiet grace), only when
+  barrel+0x98 == Sturm's self;
+  more than 3 calls in 2 ms or 400 in 1 s latches L7 (keep-awake off, Drang stays).
+- Every armed tick advances Drang's reload clock (unfocused freezes it); the
+  refill runs in an H1 invocation while S&D is eligible (the pin is per invocation).
+- A shot: one per LMB edge, 50 ms early buffer, 150 ms staleness, interval
+  clamp(1/CB3FC0(Drang), 0.2, 0.6) s. Then, in order: the invocation's pinned
+  thread (else refused and retried until stale), no akimbo lock held, the fast revalidation
+  (about 50 checked reads: Drang's root/barrel/owner/assembly 80BBC101/content,
+  variant == 3, membership, Sturm active, the private model), Sturm's state
+  (review fix), Sturm's root not disabled (CC29C0; logged only during Sturm's
+  reload), the ammo pins (with Drang's content: never Rat King),
+  loaded >= 1 (else an empty press, which starts the reload when reserve > 0),
+  reload fire-ready, the current right origin from A1F4C0 on the drawn Sturm
+  barrel (list 13D0, then 1320), shifted to Drang's muzzle by the hand's fresh
+  left frame (<= 100 ms, |p| < 0.6 m, < 20 deg) or the static pair
+  (-0.043331, 0.189999, 0.058273); CB1710 and Drang's CC29C0 logged only;
+  the EmitGate (review fix); ONE nextFiring(Drang barrel, 1, left, aux {p,1}, 1, -1, FFFFFFFF, 0, 0,
+  &progress, false, null, false); re-check; L1 on > 1 projectile, L3 on an
+  identity change, L2 on 3 consecutive ok == false. On ok: CCA120(mag, 1) with
+  loaded >= 1 re-checked (spent / unchanged counted; a mismatch latches L6),
+  CB75F0(Drang barrel, 1, the 16-aligned left frame) when the FX group passed,
+  Signals::drang_fired (the hand's one kick), an empty magazine starts the
+  reload (D = B8B7F0(root+0x2850), refill at 0.5 D through CAEB50 plus the
+  reserve fix-up, fire-ready at 0.85 D, u published; the hand is up from 0.80).
+- firing_hook routes the cached Sturm and Drang barrels before
+  firing::dispatch: one original call, never paired. A native Sturm shot
+  publishes sturm_fired and compares A1F4C0's origin with the native one (L4
+  on 3 x > 25 cm / 10 deg); a native Drang shot logs its 13 arguments.
+- Drang's own H1 is counted and serialized with our emission by the EmitGate;
+  a wait that runs out latches L8. The B7E3C0 damage summary (bootflow) feeds a 2 s
+  Drang window; magazine_hook reports Sturm's HUD magazine transitions
+  (perk_candidate) and Drang's HUD queries.
+
+Log lines (client channel; ordinary lines share a 5 lines/s budget with a
+burst of 14; install/discover/h1_probe/h1_awake/threads/summary/latch bypass
+it): ev=sd stage=install (spend, keepawake, probe_ms, remap, damage_feed),
+discover, h1_probe, h1_awake, threads, shot, native_sturm, native_drang,
+damage, sturm_mag, refuse, summary, latch; ev=akimbo stage=sd_ammo
+event=reload|transfer|transfer_fixup|transfer_failed|cancel.
+
+Tests (outputs on D:): Dawn\unit\sturm_drang_firing_tests (T1-T7, T11, T13,
+critique B2/B4/B6, ruling 13), sturm_drang_ammo_tests (design-ammo cases,
+R1/R5/R6/R8, the pins on the W2 fixture's real bytes),
+sturm_drang_discovery_tests (+T8: the fast revalidation),
+sturm_drang_runtime_tests (T10 on the real sturm_drang.cpp), and
+retained-research/build\tests2\check_sd_firing_static.py (T9 against
+text.bin and both dumps, T10 hook contracts, T12 diff) and mutate_sd2.py.
+
+## Sturm & Drang Akimbo S1: the shared scaffolding and the left hand on Drang (2026-09-26, builder 1 of 2, awaiting the firing/ammo half)
+
+Item 0xD7B8B759, private model 81A29A19 (art v5c). Sturm in the right hand
+(native), Drang in the left; RMB = Sturm, LMB = Drang, no ADS (the user,
+2026-09-24 and 2026-09-26). Spec: retained-research/INTEGRATION-S1.md
+(the lead's rulings), design-hand / design-firing / design-ammo and their
+critiques. This half (builder 1) is the scaffolding both halves share and the
+hand; the firing and ammo driver (builder 2) fills sturm_drang.cpp.
+
+Identity (identity.h/.cpp): 81A29A19 joins akimbo_model (never its
+controller-list siblings 81A29A1B/1D) and separated_model: render-copy job
+registration, the export mirror and the completed-pose resident hand merge.
+marker_bone(S&D) = 77; single_marker_model() (IKELOS, Rat King, S&D) makes
+completed_marker decode the one family-D marker. S&D stays out of
+alternating_model / alternating_firing / smg_model / sidearm_model /
+moves_weapon_root. align_sturm_drang_pose = the hand-cannon mirror with the
+1.2 m reach (pose_math.cpp).
+
+The hand (sturm_drang_pose.h, export_hook before the Thorn fallback): Sturm is
+never written (root 72, arm, 73/75/76/79). Drang is placed only by p[77],
+written on every mode-4 frame: the quiet left root while Sturm's own action
+plays (66/68/59, the same clips by clock signature, or < 0.8 s after a Sturm
+shot; released after 100 ms of idle over 120 ms; interrupts release at once;
+a draw resets), Rat King's sidearm kick on the left (the ONE kick, fed by
+Signals::drang_fired), the slide cycle (mask bit 0, DAWN_STURM_DRANG_SLIDE,
+default 1), Drang's reload lowering h(u) x 1.15 m with h(u) == 0 exactly from
+u >= 0.80 (u published by the ammo side), and marker = leftGun o S^-1 so
+drangGripOffset moves the drawn gun (critique-hand fix 1). The quiet guard is
+0.5 m for fire and 1.2 m for Sturm's reload. present_hook leaves S&D native (no
+ADS centring, no Warden sight offset, no pair lowering); fov_hook keeps the
+native field of view.
+
+Shared input (ruling 6): sturm_drang::Input {sturmShotAt, drangShotAt,
+drangReloading, drangReloadU, attached}, published lock-free through
+sturm_drang::signals() (sturm_fired / drang_fired / reload) and read as one
+snapshot in the export path. Times are precise_seconds().
+
+Install (ruling 1): the 22 baseline hooks and supported_code() are unchanged
+(hooks=22 guards=65). After they commit, install() evaluates the S&D guard
+groups (sturm_drang_guards.h: driver, ammo, fx, diagnostic; 20 rows equal to
+text.bin and both dumps, plus the relocated handler row 1D03650) with the
+checked reader and the kill file <Dawn artifact dir>\sturm-drang.off, then
+attaches H1 = CCF6A0 in its OWN Detours transaction only when the driver and
+ammo groups pass and no kill file exists. The line is
+"ev=sd stage=install result=ok|disabled reason=ok|killfile|guard_driver|
+guard_ammo|h1_attach|compiled_off hooks=0|1 groups=... killfile=0|1|unresolved
+h1=attached|failed|off hand=.. fx=.. diagnostic=.. slide=.. state=0x..". The
