+// ---- A. Firing (runtime v4a): per-gun recoil on a smoothed base --------------
+// User test of runtime v3 (2026-09-23): "the firing should alternate". The
+// native fire clip recoiled BOTH guns at every shot: the left copy renders at
+// the right gun's root, and its arm is mirrored from the right arm. Runtime v4a:
+// 1. Base: while a native fire clip may still play (a shot within
+//    fireClipSeconds) the pair rides a smoothed hold instead of the native pose.
+//    The hold is the pose on screen when the burst starts, relative to the
+//    common root 0, and tracks the live pose with a first-order low-pass
+//    (baseTrackSeconds) whose input is gated by the shot cycle: closed after
+//    each shot while the native recoil plays, opening from baseGateOpen to
+//    baseGateFull after it, when that recoil has settled (at 300 RPM the next
+//    shot comes at 0.2 s). So the base follows slow native changes (movement,
+//    turning, the fire clip's own hold) but not the 5 Hz recoil. An aim change
+//    (ADS in or out, rate baseAimRateFull per second for a full opening, held
+//    for baseAimHoldSeconds) opens the gate too and shortens the time constant
+//    to baseAimTrackSeconds, so ADS keeps close to its native pace (the recoil
+//    shows through during that transition).
+//    The left arm is re-mirrored onto the smoothed right arm (align_sidearm_pose),
+//    so the left grip stays exact. After the clip the hold blends back into the
+//    live pose over baseReleaseSeconds; a selector that ends the fire clip
+//    (interrupting_action: draw, put-away, sprint, reload) releases it over
+//    baseInterruptSeconds, and so does a live pose that leaves the base far
+//    (baseBreak*: another action such as a melee, until the next shot). With
+//    no shot in the clip window nothing changes.
+// 2. Kick: only the gun that fired kicks, in its own frame about its grip: back
+//    along the barrel (-x), up (+z), muzzle rise (about +y). Its hand and grip
+//    move rigidly with it; the elbow bends so the upper arm and forearm keep
+//    their lengths and the shoulder stays put (two-bone IK; rat_king_pose.h).
+//    Response: rise r(u)=u^2*exp(2(1-u)), u=age/kickPeakSeconds (value and
+//    velocity 0 at the shot, 1 with zero velocity at the peak), then a raised
+//    cosine back to exactly 0 over kickReturnSeconds (zero velocity at the end):
+//    C1 continuous everywhere, 0 from kickLifetimeSeconds on. At 300 RPM each
+//    gun fires every 0.4 s, so its kicks never overlap; same-gun kicks
+//    superpose, capped at kickStackLimit.
+// 3. Moving parts: the marker's mask is the bit of the gun that fired last
+//    (leftMoves or rightMoves), so only that gun's slide (75) and magazine (74)
+//    follow the native fire clip; the other gun's parts sit at their bind on
+//    its root. The bit moves at the next shot, when the native clip restarts.
+//    INFERRED: the native slide cycle ends well within the 0.2 s shot interval
+//    (clip 80BBDBB0 is 16 frames at 30 fps; its curve codec, class 80808F71, is
+//    not decoded). CAPTURE: the probe's slideSwitchMicrons (the part offset the
+//    switch drops, v5 counters) must stay near 0.
+// Reloads keep staticPairMask (both parts move with the frozen hold).
+// Runtime v4 final (review F3): a reload's recovery after a shot takes the
+// firing gun's bit once the shared parts were shown within partRestMeters of
+// their binds (translation plus 0.1 m per radian) on the frame before.
+// Projectiles and firing FX alternate per shot (dispatch_single, fired()).
+inline constexpr unsigned staticPairMask=leftMoves|rightMoves;
+inline constexpr float partRestMeters=.001f;
+inline constexpr float kickBackMeters=.035f;      // along the barrel, towards the grip
+inline constexpr float kickUpMeters=.008f;        // weapon +z
+inline constexpr float kickRiseDegrees=6.f;       // muzzle rise about the grip
+inline constexpr float kickPeakSeconds=.035f;     // rise time to the peak
+inline constexpr float kickReturnSeconds=.15f;    // raised-cosine return from the peak to rest
+inline constexpr float kickLifetimeSeconds=kickPeakSeconds+kickReturnSeconds;
+inline constexpr float kickStackLimit=1.25f;
+inline constexpr unsigned kickHistory=4;          // shots remembered per gun
+static_assert(kickLifetimeSeconds<.4f&&kickStackLimit>=1&&kickPeakSeconds<kickReturnSeconds);
+// Firing base (see 1 above). Seconds after the last shot of either gun.
+inline constexpr float baseGateOpen=.12f;         // the gate starts to open (native recoil mostly settled)
+inline constexpr float baseGateFull=.19f;         // fully open (before the next 300 RPM shot at 0.2 s)
+inline constexpr float baseTrackSeconds=.08f;     // low-pass time constant while the gate is open
+inline constexpr float baseAimRateFull=2.f;       // aim change per second that fully opens the gate
+inline constexpr float baseAimHoldSeconds=.15f;   // decay of that opening after the aim settles
+inline constexpr float baseAimTrackSeconds=.04f;  // time constant while the aim changes (ADS keeps its pace)
+inline constexpr float baseReleaseSeconds=.25f;   // back to the live pose after the fire clip
+inline constexpr float baseInterruptSeconds=.12f; // back to the live pose when another action takes over
+// The live right root this far from the base on screen (relative to root 0,
+// outside an aim change) is another action (a melee, a mantle; their
