+//   to key 46 and after key 52 (up to the last sampled key), and racked at
+//   least checkSlideMeters at key 50 when key 53 was sampled (.049);
+// - both at-rest windows shrink by the recording's sample spacing (its largest
+//   phase gap in keys, rounded up: at most 3), since a key next to a fast event
+//   (the slam, the slide's return, the head's close) holds a blend of the
+//   samples around it;
+// - the right hand (22) checkGripMin..checkGripMax from the right grip (24) on
+//   every key;
+// - complete recordings whose head was sampled (t <= recordHeadPhase,
+//   flagHeadTail): root 72 at key 66 within checkHeadTailMeters /
+//   checkHeadTailDegrees of key 0 and the left hand (21) within
+//   checkHeadTailHandMeters (the clip's head equals its tail).
+// Runtime v5, recalibrated on the live recording refused by candidate-v4-final
+// (read from the running game's Store::inProgress with the PDB; the bytes stay
+// local, only these measured values are kept):
+// - slide head: 73.2 / 56.1 / 9.5 / 0 mm at keys 0-3, at rest from key 3 to 47,
+//   racked 71.2 mm at key 51, home by 54. The head is the engine's blend out of
+//   the last fire pose (the slide back after the magazine's last round; an
+//   empty reload): the clip itself keeps the slide at rest there. Keys
+//   0..checkSlideHeadLast (6: twice the measured close, for a blend of fixed
+//   time at a faster reload, INFERRED) may hold the slide anywhere within its
+//   travel (73.2 mm measured, checkSlideTravelMeters .085 with 15 % margin);
+//   the middle (keys 7..46, the magazine out and in) and the end stay at rest.
+//   The hand-over never shows the recorded head slide (rat_king_pose.h C2).
+// - grip: .1059-.1106 m on every key (the decode gave .098-.101; v4 refused
+//   .1106 at .11). checkGripMin/Max .085-.13: ~1.3 cm below the decode's
+//   minimum and ~2 cm above the live maximum; a hand pulled 30 % off its grip
+//   (>= .13 on the synthetic clip) is still refused.
+// - head/tail: root 72 18 mm / 6.86 deg from key 0 (the head still carries the
+//   last shot's recoil), left hand 22.7 mm. checkHeadTailDegrees 10 (3 deg
+//   over the measured); the 3 cm / 4 cm limits keep their margins (18 / 22.7 mm).
+inline constexpr float checkRestMeters=.005f;
+inline constexpr unsigned checkMagazineRestLast=9,checkMagazineOutKnot=12,checkMagazineLowKnot=24;
+inline constexpr float checkMagazineOutMeters=.03f,checkMagazineLowMeters=.25f;
+inline constexpr unsigned checkSlideHeadLast=6,checkSlideFirst=47,checkSlideLast=52,checkSlideKnot=50,checkSlideSampled=53;
+inline constexpr float checkSlideMeters=.04f,checkSlideTravelMeters=.085f;
+inline constexpr float checkGripMin=.085f,checkGripMax=.13f;
+inline constexpr float checkHeadTailMeters=.03f,checkHeadTailDegrees=10.f,checkHeadTailHandMeters=.04f;
+static_assert(checkSlideHeadLast<knotRelease&&checkSlideHeadLast>=3&&checkSlideTravelMeters>.0732f&&checkSlideTravelMeters<.1f
+    &&checkGripMin<.098f&&checkGripMax>.1106f&&checkHeadTailDegrees>6.86f&&recordHeadPhase<recordArmPhase);
+// Diagnostics (akimbo.cpp): one log line per refused, aborted or declined
+// recording (and each accepted one) with the measured values
+// (rat_king_reload::Measure), at most recordLogBudget lines a session and
+// recordLogSeconds apart.
+inline constexpr unsigned recordLogBudget=48;
+inline constexpr double recordLogSeconds=1;
