+// ---- D.3 Hand-over timeline (rat_king_pose.h C2; v = the native phase, remapped
+// as the throw's from its first frame) -----------------------------------------
+// The recorded spans play handoverSpeed times faster (K). RELOAD-V4.md chose
+// 1.6 with 0.045 drops and 0.07 rises; those swing a hand or gun through the
+// view at up to ~12 m/s (offline, the synthetic test clip; a from-rest swing
+// needs ~0.08 of the clip to stay near 6.5 m/s in view). K 1.75 (within the
+// requested 1.5-1.8), drops of 0.08 and a support hand that lets go at the
+// slam (key 33; the clip holds it to key 35) put both guns up at .746, before
+// reload_5 (.803) with 0.125 s of margin at speed 1; 1.6 no longer fits.
+// Runtime v6: K = kRatKingReloadStretch x handoverSegmentRate = 1.8 on the
+// stretched reload (each magazine change at the native real-time speed):
+// slams at .222 / .544. Runtime v6 review F3: both guns up at .803 (runtime v6:
+// .734, 0.38 s before the gameplay fire-ready point reloadFireReady .85 with the
+// pair looking ready and the trigger dead), the native clip's reload_5 (the
+// native gun's slide home: its own point of looking ready), so the up-to-fire-
+// ready gap is the native fraction (.047 of the reload: 0.15 s unbuffed) and at
+// least handoverFireReadyMargin. Only E changed: the left hand's hidden return to
+// its parked gun (handoverEndRegripSpan) and the left gun's rise
+// (handoverRiseSpan) are longer.
+// Runtime v6 review F2/F8 (accepted, not changed): the magazine refills at the
+// native reloadRefill (.5 of the reload, content f0; the native clip's mag_slam
+// sound plays there too), .044 of the reload (0.14 s unbuffed) before the right
+// gun's visible slam (.544); the left gun is loaded at .222. Moving the refill
+// needs another detour (the fraction getter C9EC70 for D00BAF); moving the right
+// slam before .5 needs K >= 2.02 (a magazine change 12 % faster than native) or
+// drops and hidden spans faster than runtime v5's real-time pace (the reviewed
+// no-whip bound). rat_king_pose.h pins the lead at .05 of the reload.
+// L (left gun): the left gun plays the mirrored recording from uStart (blending
+//   in from the hold over handoverBlendIn); the right hand tucks its gun below
+//   the view (handoverTuckSpan) and parks it; the magazine drops out of the
+//   left gun; the hidden span uGone..uLow is compressed to handoverHiddenSpan
+//   while the right hand (hidden) takes the mirrored support pose; the right
+//   hand brings the magazine up and slams it in (at .228), then lets go
+//   (handoverLeave).
+// S (swap): the right hand drops (handoverDropSpan) and, hidden, returns to its
+//   parked gun (handoverRegripSpan); the loaded left gun eases to its hold.
+// R (right gun): the right gun rises from below the view (handoverRightRiseSpan) on
+//   the native recording while the left hand parks the left gun
+//   (handoverTuckLeftSpan); the left hand (hidden) takes the native support
+//   pose and slams the right magazine in (at .556).
+// E (end): the right gun eases to its hold (handoverHomeSpan); the left hand
+//   drops, returns (hidden) to its parked gun (handoverEndRegripSpan) and rises
+//   with it (handoverRiseSpan): both guns up at reload_5 (.803; runtime v4b-v5:
+//   .746 before it, runtime v6: .734; review F3 above), before fire-ready .85
+//   by handoverFireReadyMargin (handoverBothUpLimit). The swap's hidden regrip
+//   is quicker than RELOAD-V4.md's (.02, not .03); the right rise runs over most
+//   of RA at no budget cost.
+// Then the frozen hold until handoverSettleStart and a settle into the live
+// pose by handoverSettleEnd (the native gun is back at its hold by .94; v3's
+// .80 is mid-rack).
+// Tucks: the v2 shoulder swing without the wrist (arm bones 1..21 and a carried
+// gun about the upper-arm joint): tuckPitchDegrees hands down about the camera's
+// left axis, then tuckYawDegrees outward (offline, the parked guns sit about
+// 0.76 m below and 0.17 m behind the eye). Tucks and drops accelerate out of the
+// view (ease-in) and rises decelerate into it (ease-out), so the fast part of
+// each swing is below the view (a smoothstep tuck peaks near 7.6 m/s in view). The marker mask is leftMoves in L,
+// rightMoves in R and both bits otherwise; it switches only while the magazine
+// and slide are at rest (uHeadRest, runtime v5: the entry mask before it; and
+// uLeave), so the switch is invisible.
+// Runtime v6: the reload runs kRatKingReloadStretch times longer (above), so v
+// advances that many times slower in real time; K = the stretch times
+// handoverSegmentRate plays each gun's recorded magazine change at that
+// fraction of the native clip's real-time speed (1: exactly native; runtime v5
+// played 1.75 inside one native reload). The procedural spans below stay in v
+// and so slow down with the stretch (a tuck of .09 takes 0.29 s instead of
+// 0.16 s at the unbuffed 1.811 s reload).
+inline constexpr float handoverSegmentRate=1.f;
+inline constexpr float handoverSpeed=kRatKingReloadStretch*handoverSegmentRate;
+// The support hand lets go at the slam (the clip keeps it at the magazine base to uLeave).
+inline constexpr float handoverLeave=uSlam;
+inline constexpr float handoverHiddenSpan=.02f;
+inline constexpr float handoverTuckSpan=.09f;
+inline constexpr float handoverTuckLeftSpan=handoverTuckSpan; // inside RA: no budget cost (RELOAD-V4.md: .072)
+inline constexpr float handoverDropSpan=.08f;
+inline constexpr float handoverRegripSpan=.02f;      // the swap's (S), hidden: may be quick
+// Runtime v6 review F3: E's hidden return of the left hand to its parked gun
+// (runtime v6: handoverRegripSpan) and the left gun's final rise (runtime v6:
+// .09), longer so both guns come up at reload_5 (rat_king_pose.h plan: .803).
+inline constexpr float handoverEndRegripSpan=.059f;  // hidden
+inline constexpr float handoverRiseSpan=.12f;        // the left gun's final rise (0.39 s unbuffed)
+inline constexpr float handoverRightRiseSpan=.11f;   // the right gun's rise (inside RA: no budget cost)
+inline constexpr float handoverHomeSpan=.08f;
+inline constexpr float handoverBlendIn=.03f;
+inline constexpr float handoverSettleStart=.90f,handoverSettleEnd=.97f;
+// Runtime v6: both guns are up at least handoverFireReadyMargin of the reload
+// before the gameplay fire-ready point (rat_king_pose.h plan); review F3: .04
+// (runtime v6: .08), 2 frames at 30 fps even on a .9 s (buffed) native reload.
+inline constexpr float handoverFireReadyMargin=.04f;
+inline constexpr float handoverBothUpLimit=reloadFireReady-handoverFireReadyMargin; // .81 (runtime v4b-v6: .76)
+// A reload first seen later than this plays the throw (which handles late starts).
+inline constexpr float handoverLatestStart=.10f;
+inline constexpr float tuckPitchDegrees=85.f,tuckYawDegrees=12.f;
+static_assert(handoverSettleStart>reloadMarker5&&handoverSettleEnd<reloadCompletePhase+.03f&&handoverBothUpLimit<reloadFireReady
+    &&handoverLatestStart<=.1f&&handoverTuckSpan<(uGone-uStart)/handoverSpeed&&handoverLeave>uLow&&handoverLeave<=uLeave
+    &&handoverSegmentRate>=.9f&&handoverSegmentRate<=1.1f&&handoverSpeed>=1.5f&&handoverSpeed<=2.f&&recordArmPhase==handoverLatestStart);
+static_assert(handoverBothUpLimit>=reloadMarker5&&handoverSettleStart>reloadFireReady&&handoverFireReadyMargin>=.04f
+    &&handoverEndRegripSpan>=handoverRegripSpan&&handoverRiseSpan>=handoverRightRiseSpan);
+// Runtime v5, the head slide (empty vs tactical reloads). The recording's slide
+// before key checkSlideHeadLast belongs to the reload it was recorded on
+// (racked after an empty magazine's last round, at rest on a tactical reload);
+// the played keys 2..33 of the clip otherwise keep the slide at rest, and the
+// rack (keys 47-52) is never played. So the hand-over never shows a recorded
+// slide: every played slide is at rest (weaponBind3), except at the head of L,
+// where the pair starts from THIS reload's parts: the live native magazine,
+// slide and 76 (relative to root 72) on the gun(s) that showed them on the
+// frame before (the entry mask: the gun that fired last, or both when nothing
+// was written) ease to rest by uHeadRest under the entry mask, so neither
+// gun's slide pops at the start (a racked slide closes as the engine's own
+// blend closes it; a closed one stays closed, whatever the recording's head
+// held). On the frame after one that showed them at rest the mask becomes 1
+// and the mirrored recorded magazine blends in from rest by uHeadIn (the
+// clip's magazine leaves its bind at key 10). A reload whose parts are at rest
+// from the start (a tactical one) has no head: mask 1 at once, as in v4. R
+// shows the recorded magazine with the slide at rest.
+inline constexpr unsigned knotHeadRest=6,knotHeadIn=9;
+inline constexpr float uHeadRest=knotHeadRest*knotPhase,uHeadIn=knotHeadIn*knotPhase;
+static_assert(knotStart<knotHeadRest&&knotHeadRest<knotHeadIn&&knotHeadIn<knotRelease&&knotHeadRest<=checkSlideHeadLast);
+// Cancel (the action leaves 49/97, the phase restarts or drops): a
+// fast-forward to both guns up, in real seconds, towards the live aligned pose
+// of every frame (so a firing, melee or sprint pose shows as soon as each gun is
+// up; runtime v4 final, review F3: after a shot, the recoil-free firing base),
+// each side on its own:
+// - a gun in its hand (visible or tucking): arm and gun blend into the live
+//   pose over handoverHeldSeconds while the tuck unwinds (handoverHoldSeconds
+//   from the frozen hold or the settle);
+// - a parked gun whose hand is hidden: the hand returns to it hidden
+//   (handoverRegripSeconds), then rises with it into the live pose
+//   (handoverRiseSeconds);
+// - a parked gun whose hand is in view as the support hand: that hand first
+//   drops below the view (handoverDropSeconds for a full drop), then as above.
+//   A cancel is a fast-forward: these swings reach ~12 m/s on screen (the
+//   synced ones stay near 6.5 m/s);
+// - a displaced magazine or slide (mask 1 or 2) blends to rest over
+//   handoverPartSeconds (as the native cancel does); the mask then goes back to
+//   both bits and the parts blend into the live parts.
+inline constexpr float handoverHeldSeconds=.12f;
+inline constexpr float handoverHoldSeconds=.10f;
+inline constexpr float handoverRegripSeconds=.02f;
+inline constexpr float handoverRiseSeconds=.14f;
+inline constexpr float handoverDropSeconds=.09f;
+inline constexpr float handoverPartSeconds=.08f;
+static_assert(handoverDropSeconds+handoverRegripSeconds+handoverRiseSeconds<=.25f&&handoverHeldSeconds<=.15f&&handoverPartSeconds<handoverHeldSeconds);
