+// ============================================================================
+// Runtime v6 (user test of v5, 2026-09-23): "the reload during ADS is broken"
+// ============================================================================
+// ---- E.1 The ADS reload (rat_king_pose.h C2, akimbo.cpp present_hook) --------
+// What the native game does with the aim during a reload is not settled
+// (VERIFIED: the reload behaviour and D009A0 read no aim, and a reload request
+// is action 49 in every rig state; 97 needs the protected special flag; the
+// conflict rules between the aim and the reload actions are protected code).
+// Both cases are handled: (A) the aim drops to 0 at the reload and comes back
+// (while ADS is held) when the reload's blocking ends; (B) the aim stays up
+// through the reload. Before runtime v6, (B) moved the whole pair along the
+// native reload gun's swinging axis by up to adsPairOffset (present_hook reads
+// the native bone 72) and (A) brought the centring back onto the frozen HIP
+// hold (a sideways slide) when the aim returned inside the hold window; a
+// reload whose hip hold had never been seen mirrored the hip recording across
+// the ADS stance's plane. Runtime v6:
+// - the hand-over's hold and mirror plane are always a hip hold: the last
+//   non-reload frame at aim <= recordMaxAim that is not a draw (a draw frame is
+//   no stance); with none yet, the committed complete recording's last knot
+//   (the native end of a hip reload, aligned as the live pose), else the throw.
+//   Runtime v6 review F5: and a stance (stance_action below: idle, the alert
+//   idle or a known fire selector, never an interrupting one). Runtime v6 took
+//   any such frame: a sprint, a slide or a melee at the hip (sprint -> ADS ->
+//   reload: 19 cm / 43 deg off the hip stance, the left gun mirrored across the
+//   sprint gun's plane, 48 cm off, on the reviewer's synthetic sprint pose). A
+//   hip hold farther than hipKnotMeters / hipKnotDegrees (root 72 relative to
+//   root 0) from the complete recording's last knot is replaced by that knot at
+//   the hand-over's start (hipSource 4): a transition frame an aimed idle
+//   selector reports at aim <= .05 (the first ADS frame at 144 fps), or a stance
+//   the recording does not know (crouched, a gun lowered at a wall);
+// - the ADS centring is suppressed by the hand-over's weight m: present_hook
+//   shifts the frame by aim x (1 - m) x adsPairOffset. m eases 0 -> 1 with the
+//   entry blend (the ADS pose on screen -> the hip sequence) and stays 1 while
+//   the native reload plays (the settle included); once the native reload has
+//   ended (the selector leaves 49/97: the clip's end, or a cancel) it eases
+//   1 -> 0 over adsReturnSeconds of real time, frozen while a native reload
+//   plays again. Runtime v6 review F6: the tail only holds back an aim that is
+//   up; after the native reload m never exceeds aim / recordMaxAim (the running
+//   minimum from the frame before the reload ended: an aim at the hip then has
+//   no ADS stance to wait for, even when it rises on the very next frame, case
+//   A's native re-aim), so at the hip it is 0 at once (runtime v6
+//   eased it over 0.2 s even at aim 0, and an ADS pressed right after a hip
+//   reload was under-centred by up to 3.3 cm) and a later re-aim follows the
+//   native aim exactly (runtime v5's centring); the collapse never steps the
+//   presented aim by more than the native aim moved (aim (1 - aim / .05) <=
+//   .0125). VERIFIED (research\data\animation_actions.json): the action
+//   map has no ADS reload (reload_full / reload_empty -> 49 in every rig
+//   state) and the ADS stance is its own selector (idle_aim 1, fire_ads 51);
+//   INFERRED: the native ADS stance cannot show while the reload selector
+//   plays, so it comes back only after the reload, over the native aim
+//   transition (about 0.2 s, INFERRED), and the centring comes back with it.
+//   Nothing follows the native reload gun;
+// - the entry blend lasts at least handoverEntrySeconds of real time (at most
+//   handoverBlendInMax of v, which ends before the right gun's tuck:
+//   handoverTuckSpan), so an ADS start (13 cm of stance and 9.5 cm of centring
+//   offline) does not whip.
+// The throw fallback keeps runtime v5's behaviour (its hold is the pose on
+// screen at any aim, the centring follows the aim).
+inline constexpr float handoverEntrySeconds=.15f;
+inline constexpr float handoverBlendInMax=.06f;
+inline constexpr float adsReturnSeconds=.2f;
+// present_hook takes the published m only this fresh (ms), for the same
+// presentation controller; older reads 0 (the native centring). Runtime v6
+// review F9: 1000 ms (runtime v6: 100). The export republishes m on every
+// sidearm frame (0 outside a reload; a draw publishes 0 on its first export),
+// so only a hitch makes it old, and reading 0 then showed the full 9.5 cm
+// centring on an aimed hand-over for a frame after a hitch over 100 ms.
+inline constexpr unsigned long long adsSuppressFreshMs=1000;
+static_assert(handoverBlendIn<=handoverBlendInMax&&handoverBlendInMax<handoverTuckSpan&&handoverEntrySeconds>0&&adsReturnSeconds>0&&adsReturnSeconds<=.3f
+    &&adsSuppressFreshMs>=500&&adsSuppressFreshMs<=1000);
+// Runtime v6 review F5: a selector whose pose is the weapon's stance, the only
+// frames the hand-over's hip hold is taken from: idle (59 / 1 / 0), the alert
