+// ---- S2 decision 1: identity by handle; a relocation is not a rediscovery --------------
+// The S1 session log showed the S&D components RELOCATED in memory every few
+// seconds (sturm_root / drang_root change between generations while sturm_self,
+// drang_self and the content handle stay the same). A snapshot is keyed on its
+// generation-bearing handles; relocate() re-resolves the CURRENT address of each
+// requested part through the checked resolver (pool metadata read twice, the cell
+// read twice) and re-checks its identity pins at that address:
+//  - a root: the header {core tag, 80BFDFEB, definition, self, owner} and its
+//    barrel's back-reference (barrel+0x98 == self); barrel and magazine follow it;
+//  - a content record: the header {content tag, 80803AC9, definition, self, owner}
+//    and root+0x8C0 == its handle;
+//  - the active component, the private model, the equipment list and the two
+//    energy links: the header captured at discovery, field for field.
+// Each part resolves to the same address (same), to a new address with the same
+// identity (moved: the snapshot follows it) or not at all / to another identity
+// (lost: the only case that needs a new discovery). The snapshot is updated only
+// when every requested part resolved (transactional).
