+// S2 (the S1 session log, INTEGRATION-S2):
+//  1. Identity by HANDLE. The S&D components are relocated in memory every few
+//     seconds with the same handles; the input pass re-resolves the cache's roots
+//     and the active component by handle every pass (discovery::relocate), the
+//     driver re-resolves every part it touches before a shot. A relocation is
+//     not a discovery: it never drops eligibility, never bumps the generation,
+//     never counts as drang_changed. Only a handle that stops resolving or an
+//     identity pin that fails asks for a new discovery.
+//  2. The DRIVER runs in the input pass (Driver::frame, called by InputPass::pass
